:"","content":"&quot;Just for Fun,&quot; usually means not turning your post into a rant about a celebrity you don't like.<br /> <br /> Also you're factually wrong about the financial status of the movie. Box-office sales beat production, but didn't beat production + marketing + Sony's corporate culture leading to executive excess. While Sony declared it a bomb for not hitting their (ridiculously high) projected number, they've since revised a bit and admitted that they'll at least break even now - if not actually end up making money - once they factor in merchandising and all that. Blaming Ghostbusters for an increase in price of other Sony products is simply false (even if someone from Sony is saying it).<br /> <br /> For all the controversy of the film, the biggest reason it failed to meet Sony's target is because Sony failed to get the movie into China (which is how things like the MCU movies regularly hit those targets, despite controversies of creative compromises just to sate the Chinese government's desires for what foreign films are shown there). Now, it's not a surprise that Ghostbusters had trouble getting into China, but that's pretty much all in Sony's hands. If you want to make $300 million dollars in box office with a movie reliably, you need to be in China. If you don't think something can get into China, you slash it's budget to account for not getting that massive boost to box-office. Basically, a big movie should get ~$100 million in the US, ~$100 million in China, and ~$100 million everywhere else if it's performing well. Ghostbusters did that in the US and other categories, but didn't get China because it wasn't in China, so didn't hit that $300 million mark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T12:50:56-08:00","id":1006344,"title":"","content":"Well, I gotta say: you certainly spent more time thinking about the movie than I did. I thought it was terrible. Not unwatchable terrible, but just a very shitty movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T13:25:41-08:00","id":1006364,"title":"","content":"It was a franchise that really did not need a remake and, quite frankly, they would have been better off if they had just recreated the first Ghostbuster movie with the new cast. I think that the Black Furies would have welcomed a more inclusive Ghostbusters film but, just like the majority of the feminists that I know, would have been disappointed with the result. I think that, after seeing it, they would have quietly gotten on the web and panned the movie,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 11-21-2016, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T14:48:34-08:00","id":1006404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1006216-just-for-fun-what-would-the-black-furies-think-of-the-ghostbusters-2016-remake?p=1006364#post1006364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a franchise that really did not need a remake and, quite frankly, they would have been better off if they had just recreated the first Ghostbuster movie with the new cast. I think that the Black Furies would have welcomed a more inclusive Ghostbusters film but, just like the majority of the feminists that I know, would have been disappointed with the result. I think that, after seeing it, they would have quietly gotten on the web and panned the movie,</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that they're more concerned with direct threats that might arise given the outcomes of other various real world events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T15:13:09-08:00","id":1006421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1006216-just-for-fun-what-would-the-black-furies-think-of-the-ghostbusters-2016-remake?p=1006317#post1006317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all the controversy of the film, the biggest reason it failed to meet Sony's target is because Sony failed to get the movie into China...</div> </div> </div> </div>Dumb question: Did the PRC guys ever reveal <i>why</i> they blacklisted it? (Not that I care, mind. Having watched the movie, I just have difficulty imagining what about it could have ticked off the Chinese -- unless it was just their annual import limit was exceeded.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T16:19:40-08:00","id":1006457,"title":"","content":"No reason that I am aware of, though there is a subtle anti-authoritarian streak throughout the movie (much more subtle than the anti-government message of the original Ghostbusters). It could be that the translation into Mandarin made the anti-authoritarian streak more obvious, so the censors stomped on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T16:55:28-08:00","id":1006469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1006216-just-for-fun-what-would-the-black-furies-think-of-the-ghostbusters-2016-remake?p=1006421#post1006421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dumb question: Did the PRC guys ever reveal <i>why</i> they blacklisted it? (Not that I care, mind. Having watched the movie, I just have difficulty imagining what about it could have ticked off the Chinese -- unless it was just their annual import limit was exceeded.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The same (contradictory) reason why Undead-Models in &quot;World of Warcraft&quot; have to have some degree of flesh and never all-bone.<br /> <br /> Anything that <i>actively</i> promotes the ideas of &quot;Magic, Spirituality, the Supernatural and an Afterlife&quot;, if even in jest, is a HUGE No-No to the Atheist Administration of Red-Communist China. The Marvel Cinematic Universe is able to fly under the radar (thus far) because the Asgardian Powers and Infinity Stones can be explained away by (Comic Book) Science.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, this film also had the SECOND big no-no in Red-China: Weak/Negative portrayal of Chinese Culture, which was CENTRAL to the film's plot in the form of a run-down Chinese Restaurant used as the &quot;fire station&quot; and mere-background-dressing in the red-light district of town, with NOT ONE speaking Chinese onscreen.<br /> <br /> But then again, since &quot;Pirates of the Carribean&quot; got a slap on the wrist by having the racist scenes with Chow Yun Fat cut out, it may be that the Financial-Lawyers saw the train-wreck that it was going to be, and gave the &quot;standard token excuse&quot; to cut the losses before they can even happen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Back on subject:<br /> <br /> Considering the backlash and damage this film had on the image of Strong-Women (with mean-spirited and stupid backlash like <a href=\"http://i0.wp.com/theralphretort.com/wp-content/uploads/headerhey-mom.jpg?w=1080\" target=\"_blank\">http://i0.wp.com/theralphretort.com/...mom.jpg?w=1080</a> THIS occuring. WARNING: Offensive), which would no doubt have been <i>worse</i> in The World of Darkness, surely The Black Fury, even from observing the production disaster unfold online, would have done something to stop it from even occuring?<br /> <br /> On that note, since she also appeared in The Original Ghostbusters (and was press-ganged by lawyers to cameo in the remake)<br /> <br /> Would Sigourney Weaver:<br /> (1) Be a major respected/revered heroine/role-model/hero in the Black Fury Community, considering her heroic and influential portrayal of Nostromo Warrant-Officer Ellen Ripley in the <i>Alien</i> Franchise? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> (2) Heck, would she be Black Fury Kinfolk herself, if not an outright Black Fury Elder hidden in plain sight? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T19:17:43-08:00","id":1006509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1006216-just-for-fun-what-would-the-black-furies-think-of-the-ghostbusters-2016-remake?p=1006469#post1006469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Back on subject:<br /> <br /> Considering the backlash and damage this film had on the image of Strong-Women (with mean-spirited and stupid backlash like <a href=\"http://i0.wp.com/theralphretort.com/wp-content/uploads/headerhey-mom.jpg?w=1080\" target=\"_blank\">http://i0.wp.com/theralphretort.com/...mom.jpg?w=1080</a> THIS occuring. WARNING: Offensive), which would no doubt have been <i>worse</i> in The World of Darkness, surely The Black Fury, even from observing the production disaster unfold online, would have done something to stop it from even occuring?<br /> <br /> On that note, since she also appeared in The Original Ghostbusters (and was press-ganged by lawyers to cameo in the remake)<br /> <br /> Would Sigourney Weaver:<br /> (1) Be a major respected/revered heroine/role-model/hero in the Black Fury Community, considering her heroic and influential portrayal of Nostromo Warrant-Officer Ellen Ripley in the <i>Alien</i> Franchise? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (2) Heck, would she be Black Fury Kinfolk herself, if not an outright Black Fury Elder hidden in plain sight? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As a general rule, just about any given monster or reality warper is unlikely to care overly much about pop culture*. There was a slight note about Glass Walkers being concerned about the positive portrayals of vampires in fiction, and maybe kicking around a plan to counter it, but then the Red Star happened and that got bumped down to priority #10, if that. While pop culture might be used as vehicles for a message, it's unlikely to be something that Black Furies do, since the facets of society that they're trying to influence tend to be older than the film industry. They have a furtive shadow of the Catholic church that they try to work through, for example, and that alone with give them plenty of shit to deal with before you add on how they likely go on global trips to deal with threats like the Seventh Generation or even mentioning real world threats that the tribe falls upon in the night to keep them from getting theoretically worse due to banes.<br /> <br /> So, in the end, I'm going to say that any actor or actress being labeled as Garou or Fera Kin or anything of the sort is an awful lot like Al Capone being a vampire, especially one of the smaller tribes that has its work generally concentrated on everything but pop culture.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">* The Virtual Adepts are the exception that proves the rule.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T19:20:13-08:00","id":1006511,"title":"","content":"Havent seen the Film but note, that the Sailor Moon series was actuallyl meant to be feminist but some of the stuff like the &quot;Girl power&quot; speach the triad gives jadeite, is so over the top it almost parodys feminism, and many american feminists dislike it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T19:24:20-08:00","id":1006513,"title":"","content":"I personally don't see why the Furies (or any Garou outside of the Urrah tribes) would care at all about movie portrayals. I don't think the Furies as a whole care about either Ghostbusters or Sigourney Weaver. Sure you might have a cub or 2 (or more, but you get the point) that makes a big deal about either, but then the Elders point out that the world is literally dying, and the whole pop/entertainment distraction is just that.<br /> Garou can't afford to be distracted by 100% meaningless BS that we humans (for some stupid reason) allow ourselves to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T19:38:14-08:00","id":1006518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1006216-just-for-fun-what-would-the-black-furies-think-of-the-ghostbusters-2016-remake?p=1006281#post1006281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> oh my god, this forum</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I know how they'd feel about this thread. Seriously though, if they cared at all about this film it would have been about the outright sexism, hostility, and harassment that followed almost every aspect of this film. The bigger problem was the reaction to the film than the film itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T19:54:13-08:00","id":1006521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1006216-just-for-fun-what-would-the-black-furies-think-of-the-ghostbusters-2016-remake?p=1006518#post1006518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I know how they'd feel about this thread. Seriously though, if they cared at all about this film it would have been about the outright sexism, hostility, and harassment that followed almost every aspect of this film. The bigger problem was the reaction to the film than the film itself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I could thumb this up twice I would","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T21:05:24-08:00","id":1006557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1006216-just-for-fun-what-would-the-black-furies-think-of-the-ghostbusters-2016-remake?p=1006511#post1006511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Havent seen the Film but note, that the Sailor Moon series was actuallyl meant to be feminist but some of the stuff like the &quot;Girl power&quot; speach the triad gives jadeite, is so over the top it almost parodys feminism, and many american feminists dislike it.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theroguefeminist.tumblr.com/post/84348877583/atomic-glitter-alpacalicouslylovely\" target=\"_blank\">Not so cut and dried, there.</a> You'd do well to name specifics rather than vaguely say it's disliked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T21:19:39-08:00","id":1006564,"title":"","content":"To boot, many older pro-feminist works start to get a bit cringe later on - but that's because we've moved further. The same is true of depictions of homosexuality and minorities. What was once progressive and inclusive might now come off as vaguely eye-rolly or outright 'in retrospect, this comes off poorly' but at the time was a big step forward. Star Trek: TOS's periodic message of 'let's not hate people because of their colour, seriously, what the hell people' is really blatant and eye-rolly in some episodes, but at the time it was a Big Deal. Sometimes you need to drop some heavy anvils to break enough ice to let subtler takes have room to express themselves and be understood.<br /> <br /> It's also complicated by there being almost as many schools of feminist thought (or feminisms) as there are feminists. One school may view presenting a woman primarily as a happy mother and housewife as part of a regressive 'stay in your place' subtext, while another will view it as celebrating an aspect of womanhood that some women find very fulfilling, for a fairly common example. Even more confusing, both might actually be right at the same time.<br /> <br /> Oh, and then we get into the issue of different cultural conceptions of feminism and how there's a hell of a lot of annoyance coming from feminist movements in Africa, India, Asia and South America (not to mention among impoverished women and minority women in Europe, Australia, and North America) towards the tendency for the 'many american feminists' (In this context usually white, usually middle-class, and usually well-educated) to try and speak for all feminists to even further complicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T22:10:01-08:00","id":1006582,"title":"","content":"And you get oddities like Japanese, South Korean, and Taiwanese feminism, which are just different (if broadly similar) than Western feminism. Heck, women in Japan have largely stopped having sex (and children) as a protest to the socio-political pressures that they face. They would rather live with their parents than risk getting pregnant by a loser, especially since Japanese women are still expected to quit working when they have children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T07:24:44-08:00","id":1006698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1006216-just-for-fun-what-would-the-black-furies-think-of-the-ghostbusters-2016-remake?p=1006557#post1006557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://theroguefeminist.tumblr.com/post/84348877583/atomic-glitter-alpacalicouslylovely\" target=\"_blank\">Not so cut and dried, there.</a> You'd do well to name specifics rather than vaguely say it's disliked.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is just the Western view of the series, to Japanese feminists the series has its own issues. One of them is that the anime focuses much more on getting a boyfriend than the manga does. And let's not forget that there are a lot of expectations towards women in Japan that are fairly suspect. For one, the age of consent is 14, which allows portrayal of the girls that age or above be portrayed in sexualized situations.<br /> <br /> Second, the pop idol groups that are popular are heavily controlled. The girls cannot have any romantic relationships, even in their private life. Their purpose is to create a fantasy where they are 'available' for their fans. ( <a href=\"http://www.japantimes.co.jp/culture/2013/02/01/music/akb48-members-penance-shows-flaws-in-idol-culture/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.japantimes.co.jp/culture/...-idol-culture/</a> arcticle related to the subject).<br /> <br /> So, yeah, long way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T07:36:31-08:00","id":1006702,"title":"","content":"Well, individual prefectures and districts may have higher ages of consent, so it is more accurate to say that the age of consent in Japan ranges from 14-18. Combined with the prohibition against chemical birth control, it is probably better for male visitors to keep away from high school girls, as you may end up going to prison for statutory after knocking up a high school girl. The birth control issue is just another reason why Japanese women are not having sex, as that is the only steps that a woman can take under those circumstances to avoid pregnancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T07:11:47-08:00","id":1007219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1006216-just-for-fun-what-would-the-black-furies-think-of-the-ghostbusters-2016-remake?p=1006582#post1006582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you get oddities like Japanese, South Korean, and Taiwanese feminism, which are just different (if broadly similar) than Western feminism. Heck, women in Japan have largely stopped having sex (and children) as a protest to the socio-political pressures that they face. They would rather live with their parents than risk getting pregnant by a loser, especially since Japanese women are still expected to quit working when they have children.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Singles moms in japan <i>are</i> horribly mistreated the impetus behind<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Haha-Year-Japanese-Drama-English/dp/B002MKQ6PE/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1479913781&amp;sr=8-1&amp;keywords=14+sai+no+haha\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Haha-Year-Japanese-Drama-English/dp/B002MKQ6PE/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1479913781&amp;sr=8-1&amp;keywords=14+sai+no+haha\" target=\"_blank\"> Amazon.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Haha-Year-Japanese-Drama-English/dp/B002MKQ6PE/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1479913781&amp;sr=8-1&amp;keywords=14+sai+no+haha\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.amazon.com/Haha-Year-Japanese-Drama-English/dp/B002MKQ6PE/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1479913781&amp;sr=8-1&amp;keywords=14+sai+no+haha </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The subtitles can be hard to follow but its a good heartwarming show...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T07:43:44-08:00","id":1007236,"title":"","content":"Do not get me wrong, there are patriarchal aspects of American culture that are equally upsetting, but Americans do tend to encourage women to continue working after they have children. Some of the European nations (like France) have enlightened viewpoints when it comes to working mothers, but they have their own issues (like the isolation of immigrants and the unwillingness to integrate non-Whites into their communities). If we could take the best elements of each of the nations of the world and combine them into one nation, we might get a good nation, but I doubt that will happen anytime soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T13:53:17-08:00","id":1007415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1006216-just-for-fun-what-would-the-black-furies-think-of-the-ghostbusters-2016-remake?p=1006509#post1006509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in the end, I'm going to say that any actor or actress being labeled as Garou or Fera Kin or anything of the sort is an awful lot like Al Capone being a vampire, especially one of the smaller tribes that has its work generally concentrated on everything but pop culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet... John Blackfeather on page 67 of Wendigo Tribebook is exactly that: A Garou who's an actor in Hollywood.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T14:56:23-08:00","id":1007445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1006216-just-for-fun-what-would-the-black-furies-think-of-the-ghostbusters-2016-remake?p=1007415#post1007415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet... John Blackfeather on page 67 of Wendigo Tribebook is exactly that: A Garou who's an actor in Hollywood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Early edition books are weird. I would also say that he's an individual taking that route as opposed to that being a tribal pursuit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T15:13:47-08:00","id":1007454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1006216-just-for-fun-what-would-the-black-furies-think-of-the-ghostbusters-2016-remake?p=1007445#post1007445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Early edition books are weird. I would also say that he's an individual taking that route as opposed to that being a tribal pursuit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you're doing it, you're blazing a trail and can count on exactly no support from your tribe, unless it's an extraction to get you out of there and into a more straightforward fight.<br /> <br /> Well, maybe the Bone Gnawers, since they actually have some Gifts, fetishes, and totems based on their consumption of pop culture, but most of them aren't in any position to get noticed by the industry, except perhaps as fanfic authors and YouTube personalities, and even that might be stretching it. Frankweilers might occasionally get into independent press, but the more barriers there are, the less of a chance you'll see. I'd be more convinced that someone like Chuck Tingle would be a werewolf or changeling or what have you author, due to their relative anonymity and lack of public appearance, thus minimizing the chances for the Curse to kick in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T18:45:44-08:00","id":1007519,"title":"","content":"Pounded by the Physical Manifestation of my Sept's Reaction to my Last Book 'Rammed by the Ramifications of the War of Rage'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T01:24:36-08:00","id":1007612,"title":"","content":"how many diapers did you fill writing this thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3806-dwho","name":"dwho","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T04:57:56-08:00","id":1007661,"title":"","content":"To get to the actual topic of the thread, here is how I see it;<br /> <br /> Most old school Furies would be annoyed by the reliance on Weaver tech and the fact that ghosts are portrayed as nuisances. While actual ghosts are generally put to rest by garou, they do respect those gone before a lot.<br /> <br /> For the younger Furies? They'd be either very critical, or very cheerful of the film. After all, it is taking something that was very much a 'boys' thing and giving it to girls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}